title: **The Munich Rising!**
subtitle: The <span style="color: var(--kpd-colour);">Communists</span> have risen up... again.
new-page: true
view-if: year == 1919 and month == 4 and weeks == 2
priority: 1
tags: event
max-visits: 1

= The Munich Rising

<img src="img/Hoffmann_Johannes.jpeg" style="float:left; margin-right:1em; margin-bottom:0.5em; width:210px; object-fit:cover; object-position:top; border:6px solid #000000ff;"> Ever since the <span class="wide_tooltip-wrap drop-down">assasination of Kurt Eisner<span class="wide_tooltip-tip"><img src="img/kurt_eisner_assasination.jpeg">On the morning of February 21th, Kurt Eisner was shot dead by a <span style="color: var(--dnvp-colour);">nationalist</span> while on his way to tender the government's resignation, having been hit at point-blank range, making him die instantly.</span></span> in February, the <span style="color: #DDD;">B</span><span style="color: #0098D4;">a</span><span style="color: #DDD;">v</span><span style="color: #0098D4;">a</span><span style="color: #DDD;">r</span><span style="color: #0098D4;">i</span><span style="color: #DDD;">a</span><span style="color: #0098D4;">n</span> capital has been a city without a centre, its <span class="wide_tooltip-wrap drop-down">Landtag<span class="wide_tooltip-tip"><img src="img/bavarian_landtag.jpeg">The Landtag Of <span style="color: #DDD;">B</span><span style="color: #0098D4;">a</span><span style="color: #DDD;">v</span><span style="color: #0098D4;">a</span><span style="color: #DDD;">r</span><span style="color: #0098D4;">i</span><span style="color: #DDD;">a</span>, currently having been elected in February 1919 with a slight victory for the <span style="color: var(--spd-colour);">left</span>.</span></span> paralysed, its SPD Minister-President Johannes Hoffmann clinging to an authority no one obeys, and its streets given over to a ferment of soldiers' councils, striking workers, and <span style="color: var(--uspd-colour);">revolutionary clubs</span>. Word of the <span style="color: var(--kpd-colour);">Soviet Republic</span> <span class="wide_tooltip-wrap drop-down">proclaimed in Budapest<span class="wide_tooltip-tip"><img src="img/hungarian_soviet_republic.jpeg">In March 21st, a <span style="color: var(--kpd-colour);">Soviet Republic</span> was declared in Hungary, taking power from the liberal-democratic regime which was heavily unpopular due to economic pressure and strict Allied demands.</span></span> has electrified the <span style="color: var(--uspd-colour);">radicals</span>, who now insist that <span style="color: #DDD;">B</span><span style="color: #0098D4;">a</span><span style="color: #DDD;">v</span><span style="color: #0098D4;">a</span><span style="color: #DDD;">r</span><span style="color: #0098D4;">i</span><span style="color: #DDD;">a</span> too can leap straight to council rule. Against a government that cannot command its own soldiers, the pressure for a <span style="color: var(--uspd-colour);">Räterepublik</span> has become irresistible...

- @hoffmann_flee: Hoffmann flees!
- @hoffmann_stay: Hoffmann stays!

@hoffmann_flee
unavailable-subtitle: Hoffmann sees no reason for why he should flee.
subtitle: Expected.
choose-if: soldatenwehr_strengthened_1 <= 2
on-arrival: workers_kpd += 4(*1 dissent); socialism += 5

<img class="rich-image rich-image-right" decoding="async" loading="lazy" fetchpriority="auto" src="img/munich_soviet.jpeg" alt="" style="float:right; max-width:42%; margin: 0.2em 0 12px 1.25em; border: 2px solid rgb(0, 0, 0);"> And so, in the small hours, the <span style="color: var(--uspd-colour);">councils</span> have acted: the <span style="color: var(--kpd-colour);">Bavarian Soviet Republic</span> is proclaimed. Power passes to a central council of <span style="color: var(--uspd-colour);">Independent Socialists</span>, <span style="color: var(--z-colour);">Anarchists</span>, and <span style="color: var(--kpd-colour);">literary revolutionaries</span>, the playwright Ernst Toller, the anarchist philosophers Gustav Landauer and Erich Mühsam and the financier Silvio Gesell. The Hoffmann government has fled north to Bamberg, from where it declares the whole affair a usurpation. <span style="color: var(--kpd-colour);">Red</span> flags fly over the Residenz, the <span style="color: var(--z-colour);">bou</span><span style="color: var(--ddp-colour);">rg</span><span style="color: var(--dvp-colour);">eo</span><span style="color: var(--dnvp-colour);">is</span> press is silenced, the banks and barracks await orders from men who, a week ago, were writing manifestos in the cafés of Schwabing.

As always with the <span style="color: var(--uspd-colour);">Left</span>, the revolution faces challenge from within. The <span style="color: var(--kpd-colour);">Communists</span> under Eugen Leviné have refused to back the <span style="color: var(--kpd-colour);">Soviet</span>, declaring this a "pseudo-<span style="color: var(--kpd-colour);">soviet</span> of <span style="color: var(--uspd-colour);">coffeehouse communists</span>" neither arming the workers in earnest nor breaking the old order at its roots. Beyond the city, the Hoffmann Government has begun gathering loyalists to attempt to retake Munich, and it is expected Reichswehr Minister Gustav Noske will authorize the Freikorps to supplement Hoffmann's forces.

- @root: Pointless bloodshed.


@hoffmann_stay
subtitle: Surprising.
view-if: soldatenwehr_strengthened_1 >= 2
on-arrival: workers_uspd += 4(*1 dissent); pro_republic += 5

Unfortunately for the <span style="color: var(--kpd-colour);">Communists</span>, Hoffmann has elected to stay in <span style="color: #DDD;">B</span><span style="color: #0098D4;">a</span><span style="color: #DDD;">v</span><span style="color: #0098D4;">a</span><span style="color: #DDD;">r</span><span style="color: #0098D4;">i</span><span style="color: #DDD;">a</span>, leading to a crowd of <span style="color: var(--kpd-colour);">Communists</span> surrounding the Residenz, led by Ernst Toller. The crowd has demanded Hoffmann's immediate resignation, and the immediate creation of a "<span style="color: #DDD;">B</span><span style="color: #0098D4;">a</span><span style="color: #DDD;">v</span><span style="color: #0098D4;">a</span><span style="color: #DDD;">r</span><span style="color: #0098D4;">i</span><span style="color: #DDD;">a</span><span style="color: #0098D4;">n</span> <span style="color: var(--kpd-colour);">Soviet Republic</span>", however Hoffmann has refused citing the un<span style="color: var(--ddp-colour);">democratic</span> nature of these demands. Moreover, elements of the <span style="color: var(--reichsbanner-colour);">Republikanischer Soldatenwehr</span> were alerted by <span class="wide_tooltip-wrap">Martin Segitz<span class="wide_tooltip-tip"><span style="color: var(--spd-colour);">**SPD**</span> <span style="color: #DDD;">B</span><span style="color: #0098D4;">a</span><span style="color: #DDD;">v</span><span style="color: #0098D4;">a</span><span style="color: #DDD;">r</span><span style="color: #0098D4;">i</span><span style="color: #DDD;">a</span> Interior Minister</span></span> leading to an immediate deployment into the city center, preventing the <span style="color: var(--kpd-colour);">Communists</span> from storming the building. Worse still, many of the <span style="color: var(--uspd-colour);">councils</span> have refused to support the <span style="color: var(--kpd-colour);">Revolution</span> citing the Cabinet's acceptance of the <span style="color: var(--spd-colour);">socialization</span> demands made by the Berlin Soviet last month, and thus have refused to lend their support to the Revolutionaries.

- @yay_nice_we_win: Ultimately, the "revolution" fizzles out.

@yay_nice_we_win

Without major support, isolated and surrounded by <span style="color: var(--z-colour);">Rep</span><span style="color: var(--spd-colour);">ubli</span><span style="color: var(--ddp-colour);">can</span> forces, the <span style="color: var(--kpd-colour);">communist</span> mob has dissolved, with planned revolts by the KPD at the Central Station and other key government buildings being cancelled following <span style="color: var(--reichsbanner-colour);">Soldatenwehr</span> reinforcements arriving from the north. This event has secured Ebert's support for the <span style="color: var(--reichsbanner-colour);">Soldatenwehr</span>, despite cries from many calling for its disbandment.

- @root: It seems like the <span style="color: var(--reichsbanner-colour);">Soldatenwehr</span> have proven their utility.

